    "q-225155": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225155",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$-50{x}^{2}+50x-8=$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to factor the following expression:\n\n$$\n-50{x}^{2}+50x-8\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all the terms have a common factor of $-2.$ So, we can simplify the calculation by first factoring out $-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(25{x}^{2}-25x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the trinomial $25{x}^{2}-25x+4$ in parentheses. To do this, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant (which is $25\\times 4=100$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient (which is $-25$).\n\nSince the linear coefficient is negative and the constant is positive, we only need to consider the *negative* factor pairs of $100.$\n\nThe negative factor pairs of $100$ are\n\n$$\n(-1,-100),\\,(-2,-50),\\,(-4,-25),\\,(-5,-20),\\,(-10,-10).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-5,-20)$ add to $-25:$ \n\n$$\n-5-20=-25\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-5x-20x,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-25x+4 & = \\\\ 25{x}^{2}-5x-20x+4 & = \\\\ (25{x}^{2}-5x)-(20x-4) & = \\\\ 5x(5x-1)-4(5x-1) & = \\\\ (5x-4)(5x-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original trinomial factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(5x-4)(5x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-225155-a",
